Specification Investments

Description Tracking what an investment account is currently worth, without
Description tracking lots, holding periods or realised gains.
Details
Details SCOPE. The first round is about spending reports. No report in this file
Details is compared against Quicken in that round, and the holdings report at
Details the end of it is the last thing to build, not the first.
Details
Details What is in scope is everything in here that a spending report depends
Details on, and that is more than it looks. The 899 investment records in the
Details business file include dividends, which post to an income category, and
Details fees, which post to an expense one. Those reach the spending report and
Details must be right. So must the rule that sends a revaluation to
Details Equity:Market Value Changes, because its whole purpose is to keep market
Details movement out of that report.
Details
Details What can wait is the holdings report, the staleness marking, and
Details recording prices at all. A migrated book has no price list to work from
Details anyway, so every holding starts stale and the balances are as good as
Details the last transaction makes them. See ImportQif and
Details AcceptanceAgainstQuicken.
Details
Details What is wanted here is the current balance. Cost basis, holding periods
Details and realised gain or loss are reported on the 1099, and keeping a second
Details set of those figures here would mean maintaining something that has to
Details agree with a document nobody controls. So they are not kept.
Details
Details What is kept must still balance, because the book is double entry
Details throughout and net worth is read off the real accounts. A security is
Details therefore an account of type Investment beneath the brokerage account,
Details carrying a money balance like any other, and a share count beside it.
Details When a price changes, the difference is posted against
Details Equity:Market Value Changes. Equity is nominal, so a revaluation moves
Details net worth without ever appearing in a report of income and expenses.
Details That is the whole of the design, and it is what the simplification buys.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The shape of a brokerage account
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Background A brokerage account with two holdings
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                           | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Brokerage               | Investment | true        |
| Assets:Brokerage:Cash          | Investment | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX         | Investment | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B         | Investment | false       |
| Assets:Checking                | Bank       | false       |
| Income:Dividends               | Income     | false       |
| Income:Interest                | Income     | false       |
| Expenses:Investment:Fees       | Expense    | false       |
| Equity:Market Value Changes    | Equity     | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances        | Equity     | false       |

Entity Holding
Description The share count and price of one security, beside the account that
Description carries its value.
Details Value is not stored. It is the money balance of the account, and the
Details invariant below is what keeps the two in step.
Details A security is identified by its name. The symbol is optional, because a
Details QIF export generally has none: see the naming rule below.
| Attribute    | Type         | Default    | Notes                         |
| Account      | AccountPath  |            | The Investment account for it |
| SecurityName | SecurityName |            | The identifier                |
| Symbol       | Symbol       | none       | Optional shorthand            |
| Shares       | Shares       | 0          |                               |
| Price        | Price        | 0          | The last price recorded       |
| PriceAsOf    | Date         | 2024-01-01 | When that price was recorded  |

BusinessRule What the account of a holding is called
Description The symbol where there is one, because it is shorter and is what a
Description holdings report is read by. The name otherwise.
Details Colons are replaced, as for any account name. A name of 76 characters
Details makes a long path, and that is preferred to inventing a symbol that
Description would then disagree with every statement.
Examples: HoldingAccountName
| SecurityName                   | Symbol | AccountName                    |
| Vanguard Total Stock Mkt Idx   | VTSAX  | VTSAX                          |
| ISHARES U S TRANSPORTATION ETF |        | ISHARES U S TRANSPORTATION ETF |
| Berkshire Hathaway B           | BRK.B  | BRK.B                          |

Attributes HoldingAccountName
| Attribute    | Type         | Default |
| SecurityName | SecurityName |         |
| Symbol       | Symbol       | none    |
| AccountName  | AccountName  |         |

Collection Holdings
| DataType | Minimum | Maximum | Notes                        |
| Holding  | 0       | 10000   | One per Investment account   |

BusinessRule The value of a holding is its shares times its price
Description And that value is the money balance of its account. Every operation
Description below leaves this true; it is checked whenever the file is opened.
Details Rounding is to the cent, half away from zero.
Examples: HoldingValue
| Shares     | Price    | Value    | Notes                          |
| 100        | 123.4500 | 12345.00 |                                |
| 0          | 123.4500 | 0.00     | A closed position              |
| 100        | 0        | 0.00     | Unpriced                       |
| 12.345678  | 100.0000 | 1234.57  | Rounded up to the cent         |
| 12.344444  | 100.0000 | 1234.44  | Rounded down                   |
| 3          | 0.3333   | 1.00     | 0.9999 rounds to one           |

Attributes HoldingValue
| Attribute | Type   | Default |
| Shares    | Shares | 0       |
| Price     | Price  | 0       |
| Value     | Money  | 0.00    |
| Notes     | String | none    |

Scenario The balance of a brokerage account is its cash and its holdings
Description The brokerage account itself is a placeholder, so its balance is the
Description roll-up of the cash account and the holdings beneath it, which is
Description the ordinary rule from Accounts and needs nothing special here.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 110.0000 | 2024-06-28 |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | BRK.B  | 10     | 405.0000 | 2024-06-28 |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                | Amount   |
| T1  | 2024-01-02 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2500.00  |
| T1  | 2024-01-02 | Equity:Opening Balances | -2500.00 |
| T2  | 2024-01-03 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 11000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-01-03 | Equity:Opening Balances | -11000.00 |
| T3  | 2024-01-03 | Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | 4050.00  |
| T3  | 2024-01-03 | Equity:Opening Balances | -4050.00 |
Then rolled up balances are : RolledUpBalance
| Account                | OwnBalance | TotalBalance | Notes            |
| Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2500.00    | 2500.00      | Uninvested cash  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 11000.00   | 11000.00     | 100 at 110.00    |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | 4050.00    | 4050.00      | 10 at 405.00     |
| Assets:Brokerage       | 0.00       | 17550.00     | Cash and holdings |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Buying and selling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Attributes TradeEntry
Description What is typed to record a trade.
| Attribute | Type        | Default    |
| Account   | AccountPath |            |
| Date      | Date        | 2024-01-01 |
| Symbol    | Symbol      |            |
| Shares    | Shares      | 0          |
| Price     | Price       | 0          |
| Fee       | Money       | 0.00       |
| Proceeds  | Money       | 0.00       |

Scenario Buying shares moves cash into the holding
Description Two postings, and no gain to compute. The holding is carried at
Description what was paid for it until a price is recorded.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 0      | 0     | 2024-01-01 |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                 | Amount    |
| T1  | 2024-01-02 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash   | 20000.00  |
| T1  | 2024-01-02 | Equity:Opening Balances | -20000.00 |
When shares bought : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date    | 2024-02-01             |
| Symbol  | VTSAX                  |
| Shares  | 100                    |
| Price   | 100.0000               |
Then postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                | Amount    |
| T2  | 2024-02-01 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 10000.00  |
| T2  | 2024-02-01 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | -10000.00 |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-02-01 |

Scenario A commission is an expense, not part of the holding
Description Folding the fee into the value of the holding would make the
Description invariant false, because the shares did not cost more than their
Description price. It is a three-posting transaction.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | BRK.B  | 0      | 0     | 2024-01-01 |
Given postings are as previous
When shares bought : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B |
| Date    | 2024-02-01             |
| Symbol  | BRK.B                  |
| Shares  | 10                     |
| Price   | 400.0000               |
| Fee     | 6.95                   |
Then postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                  | Amount   |
| T2  | 2024-02-01 | Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B   | 4000.00  |
| T2  | 2024-02-01 | Expenses:Investment:Fees | 6.95     |
| T2  | 2024-02-01 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash    | -4006.95 |

Scenario Buying more shares averages the price, because no lots are kept
Description This is the simplification. Two purchases at different prices leave
Description one holding at one price, and that price is the carrying value
Description divided by the shares. It is not a cost basis and is not used as
Description one: the 1099 has the basis.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-02-01 |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                 | Amount    |
| T1  | 2024-01-02 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash   | 20000.00  |
| T1  | 2024-01-02 | Equity:Opening Balances | -20000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-02-01 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX  | 10000.00  |
| T2  | 2024-02-01 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash   | -10000.00 |
When shares bought : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date    | 2024-03-01             |
| Symbol  | VTSAX                  |
| Shares  | 50                     |
| Price   | 120.0000               |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 150    | 106.6667 | 2024-03-01 |
Then balances are : AccountBalance
| Account                | RawBalance | DisplayBalance | Notes                   |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 16000.00   | 16000.00       | 10000.00 plus 6000.00   |

BusinessRule How the carried price changes when more shares are bought
Description The new price is the total carried value divided by the total shares,
Description rounded to four places. The value is the sum of what was paid; the
Description price is derived from it, so the invariant holds.
Examples: AveragePrice
| HeldShares | HeldValue | BoughtShares | BoughtPrice | NewShares | NewValue | NewPrice | Notes               |
| 100        | 10000.00  | 50           | 120.0000    | 150       | 16000.00 | 106.6667 |                     |
| 0          | 0.00      | 100          | 100.0000    | 100       | 10000.00 | 100.0000 | A first purchase    |
| 100        | 10000.00  | 100          | 100.0000    | 200       | 20000.00 | 100.0000 | Same price          |
| 3          | 100.00    | 1            | 1.0000      | 4         | 101.00   | 25.2500  | Rounds to four places |

Attributes AveragePrice
| Attribute    | Type   | Default |
| HeldShares   | Shares | 0       |
| HeldValue    | Money  | 0.00    |
| BoughtShares | Shares | 0       |
| BoughtPrice  | Price  | 0       |
| NewShares    | Shares | 0       |
| NewValue     | Money  | 0.00    |
| NewPrice     | Price  | 0       |
| Notes        | String | none    |

Scenario Selling shares at the carried price needs no gain
Description The holding is carried at 106.6667 and sold at that price, so the
Description cash in equals the value out and there is nothing left over.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 150    | 106.6667 | 2024-03-01 |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                 | Amount    |
| T1  | 2024-03-01 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX  | 16000.00  |
| T1  | 2024-03-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | -16000.00 |
When shares sold : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date    | 2024-04-01             |
| Symbol  | VTSAX                  |
| Shares  | 50                     |
| Price   | 106.6667               |
Then postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                | Amount    |
| T2  | 2024-04-01 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 5333.34   |
| T2  | 2024-04-01 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | -5333.34  |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 106.6666 | 2024-04-01 |
# The price is re-derived from the value that is left, 10666.66 over 100
# shares, rather than carried forward, so the invariant stays exact.

Scenario Selling above the carried price puts the difference to Equity
Description The difference is a market value change, not income, so it does not
Description appear in a report of income and expenses. It is also not a realised
Description gain for tax: that figure comes on the 1099.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                 | Amount    |
| T1  | 2024-03-01 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX  | 10000.00  |
| T1  | 2024-03-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | -10000.00 |
When shares sold : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date    | 2024-04-01             |
| Symbol  | VTSAX                  |
| Shares  | 100                    |
| Price   | 130.0000               |
Then postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                     | Amount    |
| T2  | 2024-04-01 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash       | 13000.00  |
| T2  | 2024-04-01 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX      | -10000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-04-01 | Equity:Market Value Changes | -3000.00  |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 0      | 130.0000 | 2024-04-01 |

Scenario Selling more shares than are held is refused
Description Short positions are not modelled, so this is always either a missing
Description purchase or a typing mistake, and both are worth stopping for.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
When shares sold : TradeEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date    | 2024-04-01             |
| Symbol  | VTSAX                  |
| Shares  | 150                    |
| Price   | 130.0000               |
Then rejected because : Rejection
| Reason                                        |
| Only 100 shares of VTSAX are held             |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recording a price
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario Recording a new price revalues the holding
Description This is how the balance is kept current, and it is the only thing
Description that has to be done regularly for the figures to mean anything.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                 | Amount    |
| T1  | 2024-03-01 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX  | 10000.00  |
| T1  | 2024-03-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | -10000.00 |
When price recorded : PriceEntry Vertical
| Symbol | VTSAX      |
| Price  | 110.0000   |
| AsOf   | 2024-06-28 |
Then postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                     | Amount   |
| T2  | 2024-06-28 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX      | 1000.00  |
| T2  | 2024-06-28 | Equity:Market Value Changes | -1000.00 |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 110.0000 | 2024-06-28 |
Then balances are : AccountBalance
| Account                | RawBalance | DisplayBalance | Notes            |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 11000.00   | 11000.00       | 100 at 110.00    |

Attributes PriceEntry
| Attribute | Type   | Default    |
| Symbol    | Symbol |            |
| Price     | Price  | 0          |
| AsOf      | Date   | 2024-01-01 |

Scenario A price that falls revalues downwards
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are as previous
Given postings are as previous
When price recorded : PriceEntry Vertical
| Symbol | VTSAX      |
| Price  | 90.0000    |
| AsOf   | 2024-06-28 |
Then postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                     | Amount   |
| T2  | 2024-06-28 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX      | -1000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-06-28 | Equity:Market Value Changes | 1000.00  |

Scenario Recording the price already held posts nothing
Description A revaluation of zero is not worth a transaction, and a register
Description full of them would hide the ones that matter.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are as previous
Given postings are as previous
When price recorded : PriceEntry Vertical
| Symbol | VTSAX      |
| Price  | 100.0000   |
| AsOf   | 2024-06-28 |
Then postings created are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date | Account | Amount |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-06-28 |
# The date is still brought forward: the price was confirmed on the 28th.

Scenario A price applies to every account holding that symbol
Description The same fund held in two accounts is priced once. The revaluation
Description is one transaction per holding, because each holding is its own
Description account and a posting belongs to one.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                        | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Brokerage            | Investment | true        |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX      | Investment | false       |
| Assets:IRA                  | Investment | true        |
| Assets:IRA:VTSAX            | Investment | false       |
| Equity:Market Value Changes | Equity     | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances     | Equity     | false       |
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
| Assets:IRA:VTSAX       | VTSAX  | 50     | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                 | Amount    |
| T1  | 2024-03-01 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX  | 10000.00  |
| T1  | 2024-03-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | -10000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-03-01 | Assets:IRA:VTSAX        | 5000.00   |
| T2  | 2024-03-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | -5000.00  |
When price recorded : PriceEntry Vertical
| Symbol | VTSAX      |
| Price  | 110.0000   |
| AsOf   | 2024-06-28 |
Then postings created are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                     | Amount   |
| T3  | 2024-06-28 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX      | 1000.00  |
| T3  | 2024-06-28 | Equity:Market Value Changes | -1000.00 |
| T4  | 2024-06-28 | Assets:IRA:VTSAX            | 500.00   |
| T4  | 2024-06-28 | Equity:Market Value Changes | -500.00  |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Income from investments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario A dividend paid in cash is income
Description Dividends and interest are income and belong in an income report,
Description because they are taxable and because the question of how much the
Description investments paid is worth answering. Only the market movement is
Description kept out of that report.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are as previous
When dividend recorded : IncomeEntry Vertical
| Account  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date     | 2024-06-30             |
| Symbol   | VTSAX                  |
| Amount   | 250.00                 |
| Category | Income:Dividends       |
| Reinvest | false                  |
Then postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account               | Amount  |
| T5  | 2024-06-30 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash | 250.00  |
| T5  | 2024-06-30 | Income:Dividends      | -250.00 |

Attributes IncomeEntry
| Attribute | Type        | Default    |
| Account   | AccountPath |            |
| Date      | Date        | 2024-01-01 |
| Symbol    | Symbol      |            |
| Amount    | Money       | 0.00       |
| Category  | AccountPath |            |
| Reinvest  | Boolean     | false      |
| Shares    | Shares      | 0          |
| Price     | Price       | 0          |

Scenario A reinvested dividend is income and a purchase at once
Description Still income, so it still appears in an income report, and the cash
Description never rests in the cash account. The shares go up and the carried
Description price is re-derived.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                 | Amount    |
| T1  | 2024-03-01 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX  | 10000.00  |
| T1  | 2024-03-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | -10000.00 |
When dividend recorded : IncomeEntry Vertical
| Account  | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Date     | 2024-06-30             |
| Symbol   | VTSAX                  |
| Amount   | 250.00                 |
| Category | Income:Dividends       |
| Reinvest | true                   |
| Shares   | 2.5                    |
| Price    | 100.0000               |
Then postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                | Amount  |
| T2  | 2024-06-30 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 250.00  |
| T2  | 2024-06-30 | Income:Dividends       | -250.00 |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 102.5  | 100.0000 | 2024-06-30 |

Scenario Investment income shows in an income report and market movement does not
Description The two scenarios above and a revaluation, reported together. This
Description is what the choice of Equity for revaluation buys, and it is the
Description reason the choice was made.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                     | Amount   |
| T1  | 2024-06-30 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash       | 250.00   |
| T1  | 2024-06-30 | Income:Dividends            | -250.00  |
| T2  | 2024-06-30 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash       | 12.00    |
| T2  | 2024-06-30 | Income:Interest             | -12.00   |
| T3  | 2024-06-28 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX      | 1000.00  |
| T3  | 2024-06-28 | Equity:Market Value Changes | -1000.00 |
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2024-01-01 |
| To       | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account          | Level | Amount | IsSubtotal |
| Income           | 0     | 262.00 | true       |
| Income:Dividends | 1     | 250.00 | false      |
| Income:Interest  | 1     | 12.00  | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 262.00 |
| TotalExpenses | 0.00   |
| Net           | 262.00 |
# The 1000.00 revaluation is absent, and net worth is 1000.00 higher for it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An account tracked by value alone
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario An account may carry a stated value with no holdings at all
Description A pension or an employer plan reports one figure on one statement
Description and the positions behind it are not worth entering. The account
Description holds no holdings; its value is set directly, against the same
Description equity account a revaluation uses.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                        | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Pension              | Investment | false       |
| Equity:Market Value Changes | Equity     | false       |
| Equity:Opening Balances     | Equity     | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                 | Amount    |
| T1  | 2024-01-01 | Assets:Pension          | 85000.00  |
| T1  | 2024-01-01 | Equity:Opening Balances | -85000.00 |
When value stated : ValueEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Pension |
| Value   | 91200.00       |
| AsOf    | 2024-06-30     |
Then postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                     | Amount   |
| T2  | 2024-06-30 | Assets:Pension              | 6200.00  |
| T2  | 2024-06-30 | Equity:Market Value Changes | -6200.00 |
Then balances are : AccountBalance
| Account        | RawBalance | DisplayBalance | Notes             |
| Assets:Pension | 91200.00   | 91200.00       | As last stated    |

Attributes ValueEntry
| Attribute | Type        | Default    |
| Account   | AccountPath |            |
| Value     | Money       | 0.00       |
| AsOf      | Date        | 2024-01-01 |

Scenario A stated value on an account that has holdings is refused
Description The value of such an account is the total of its holdings. Setting
Description it directly would make the invariant false and there would be no way
Description to tell which figure was wrong.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                        | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX      | Investment | false       |
| Equity:Market Value Changes | Equity     | false       |
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 100.0000 | 2024-03-01 |
When value stated : ValueEntry Vertical
| Account | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX |
| Value   | 11000.00               |
| AsOf    | 2024-06-30             |
Then rejected because : Rejection
| Reason                                                               |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX holds VTSAX; record a price instead of a value |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is deliberately absent
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario No realised gain is reported, by design
Description Asking for a gain report says what the program does instead, rather
Description than offering a figure that would not agree with the 1099 and would
Description be believed anyway.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
When gain report requested
Then told that : Notice
| Message                                                                        |
| Realised gains are not tracked; the carried price is an average, not a basis   |

Attributes Notice
| Attribute | Type | Default |
| Message   | Text |         |

Scenario A holdings report shows what is held now, and when it was priced
Description The age of a price is shown beside it, because a balance resting on
Description a price from two years ago is worth distrusting and there is no way
Description to tell from the figure alone.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Brokerage       | Investment | true        |
| Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | Investment | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | Investment | false       |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | Investment | false       |
Given today is : Today Vertical
| Date | 2024-07-01 |
Given holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price    | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 100    | 110.0000 | 2024-06-28 |
| Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | BRK.B  | 10     | 405.0000 | 2022-01-14 |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                | Amount   |
| T1  | 2024-01-02 | Assets:Brokerage:Cash  | 2500.00  |
| T2  | 2024-01-03 | Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | 11000.00 |
| T3  | 2024-01-03 | Assets:Brokerage:BRK.B | 4050.00  |
When holdings report run
Then holdings report rows are : HoldingsReportRow
| Symbol | Shares | Price    | Value    | PriceAsOf  | DaysOld | Stale |
| BRK.B  | 10     | 405.0000 | 4050.00  | 2022-01-14 | 899     | true  |
| VTSAX  | 100    | 110.0000 | 11000.00 | 2024-06-28 | 3       | false |
Then holdings report total is : HoldingsTotal Vertical
| Cash       | 2500.00  |
| Securities | 15050.00 |
| Total      | 17550.00 |

Attributes HoldingsReportRow
Description A holding is listed by its symbol where it has one and by its name
Description otherwise, so both columns are here and one of them may be empty.
| Attribute    | Type         | Default    |
| SecurityName | SecurityName | none       |
| Symbol       | Symbol       | none       |
| Shares       | Shares       | 0          |
| Price        | Price        | 0          |
| Value        | Money        | 0.00       |
| PriceAsOf    | Date         | 2024-01-01 |
| DaysOld      | Integer      | 0          |
| Stale        | Boolean      | false      |

Attributes HoldingsTotal
| Attribute  | Type  | Default |
| Cash       | Money | 0.00    |
| Securities | Money | 0.00    |
| Total      | Money | 0.00    |

BusinessRule When a price is called stale
Description Thirty days, which is long enough that a monthly statement keeps a
Description holding fresh and short enough that a forgotten one is noticed.
Examples: Staleness
| DaysOld | Stale | Notes                        |
| 0       | false | Priced today                 |
| 30      | false | The last day it is fresh     |
| 31      | true  |                              |
| 899     | true  |                              |

Attributes Staleness
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| DaysOld   | Integer | 0       |
| Stale     | Boolean | false   |
| Notes     | String  | none    |
